{
  "schema": "lrm.vkgen.bindings/1",
  "about": "The single list of what Lrm.Gpu.Vulkan.Interop binds (VulkanInteropApi contract, docs/contracts/vulkan-interop.md). tools/vkgen reads it with the pinned vk.xml and writes the generated files; the ABI oracle (tools/abi-oracle/vulkan) checks every item the generated assembly holds. Core versions up to coreVersion and the listed extensions decide which enum values, sType values and extension constants are bound and which providers a command has. structs, enums, funcpointers and commands are roots: the generator adds every type they reach by value (struct members, union members, array elements, enum and bitmask types, handles) and, for commands, the structs their pointer parameters point to. Pointer members stay nativeint and pull nothing in. Add an item here, regenerate (dotnet run --project tools/vkgen/Lrm.Tools.VkGen -c Release), then refresh the oracle (pwsh tools/abi-oracle/vulkan/run.ps1 -Update), all in one commit.",
  "registry": {
    "toolchainEntry": "vkxml",
    "note": "The vk.xml pin (version, size, SHA-256, install path under LRM_DATA) is the vkxml entry of tools/bootstrap/toolchain.json; the generator verifies the SHA-256 before reading."
  },
